hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2914","###\n Muhammad bin Abd al-A'la narrated to us, stating that Khalid (meaning Ibn al-Harith) narrated to us. In another narration, Muhammad bin Bashshar narrated to us, stating that Muhammad narrated to us. They both said: Shu'bah narrated to us. In yet another narration, Abu Musa narrated to us, stating that Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan and Shu'bah. This is the narration of al-San'ani (Sufyan), who stated that Salam"
"2915","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Qaysi: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us; Jarir narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Hujayyah ibn Adi, that a man asked 'Ali (RA) about the cow (in the context of sacrifice). He said, \"It should be seven years old.\" The man asked, \"What about the horn?\" He replied, \"That will not harm you.\" The man asked, \"What about the lame?\" He replied, \"If it has reached the place of sacrifice.\" Then he said, \"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had commanded us to inspect the eye and the ear (for defects).\"\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
